# What `npm pack` leaves out of the package tarball (OpenUPM builds its package this way, #6, #101).
# A Git URL install clones the whole repository instead; Unity skips `~` and dot folders there too.
# Shipped: Runtime/, Editor/, Plugins/, Tests/, Samples~/, Documentation~/, package.json, README,
# CHANGELOG, LICENSE, Third-Party Notices, AGENTS/CLAUDE/CONTRIBUTING (public repo), and their .meta files.

# Internal docs, dev tooling, CI and agent configuration
Development~/
Tools~/
.claude/
.github/
.githooks/
.config/
.editorconfig
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.npmignore

# Local build output (also in .gitignore, which npm ignores when this file exists)
.build/
.tools/
__pycache__/
Library/
Logs/
Temp/
Obj/
Build/
Builds/
UserSettings/
MemoryCaptures/
.vscode/
.vs/
.DS_Store
*.csproj
*.sln
*.pdb
Tests/Benchmarks/*.observed.json
